      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CHEYNE BAY (1) is the horse to beat after missing by a nose first-up at this track in CL5 grade, and that effort had extra merit after he began slowly and had trouble getting clear from the 200m. He'll be better for that effort and may be able to sit closer today from a better draw. Ticks plenty of boxes here second-up. MORIAH (9) brings winning form from Kalgoorlie, where she beat Luminous Lady by a length and a half in a CL2 after being tightened at the start. The sting out of the ground won't hurt and she makes plenty of appeal with no weight on her back. CHINO BAY (4) was only beaten a length and a half when resuming at Ascot and has a previous win at this distance, with her G3 WA Oaks run two back giving the profile more depth than the recent finishing position shows. VANCOUVER STORM (7) has been runner-up in his past two, is proven at this track and distance, and the apprentice claim keeps him right in the mix. COSTA DEL DARLO (3) can repeat the dose without surprising.",
